{"name":"Vegetarian Vulture","hex":"#cccc99","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vegetarian","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who does not eat animal flesh, or, in some cases, use any animal products. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An animal that eats only plants; a herbivore."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to the type of diet eaten by vegetarians (in all senses).","Without meat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vegetarian"},{"term":"vulture","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several carrion-eating birds of the families Accipitridae and Cathartidae.","A person who profits from the suffering of others."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To circle around one's target as if one were a vulture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vulture"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vegetarianism","blocks":[{"text":"Vegetarianism is the practice of abstaining from the consumption of meat. It may also include abstaining from eating all by-products of animal slaughter. A person who practices vegetarianism is known as a vegetarian."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Soy-whey-protein-diet.jpg/330px-Soy-whey-protein-diet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vegetarianism","wikidata":"Q83364"},{"title":"Vulture","blocks":[{"text":"A vulture is a bird of prey that scavenges on carrion. There are 23 extant species of vulture. Old World vultures include 16 living species native to Europe, Africa, and Asia; New World vultures are native to North and South America and consist of seven species.\nA particular characteristic of many vultures is a bald, unfeathered head. This bare skin is thought to keep the head clean when feeding, and also plays an important role in thermoregulation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Gyps_rueppellii_-Nairobi_National_Park%2C_Kenya-8-4c.jpg/330px-Gyps_rueppellii_-Nairobi_National_Park%2C_Kenya-8-4c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vulture","wikidata":"Q123120"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Tirthankar_Parshvanath_Bhagwan.jpg/500px-Tirthankar_Parshvanath_Bhagwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Tirthankar_Parshvanath_Bhagwan.jpg/500px-Tirthankar_Parshvanath_Bhagwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Parshwanatha founded Jain vegetarianism in the 9th century BCE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATirthankar_Parshvanath_Bhagwan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Emperor_Tenmu.jpg/500px-Emperor_Tenmu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Emperor_Tenmu.jpg/1280px-Emperor_Tenmu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Emperor_Tenmu.jpg/500px-Emperor_Tenmu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Emperor Tenmu began bans on the  killing for and eating of meat in 675 CE in Japan.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEmperor_Tenmu.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Vegan_Gardein_Tofu_Foods_Display_%28cropped1%29.jpg/500px-Vegan_Gardein_Tofu_Foods_Display_%28cropped1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Vegan_Gardein_Tofu_Foods_Display_%28cropped1%29.jpg/1280px-Vegan_Gardein_Tofu_Foods_Display_%28cropped1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_co